From cee496ae9b17298218f78a2dba37734ecdfe1d0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven Williams <stevenwritescode@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:03:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(scripts): fire close when a script WebSocket fails to
 connect on the server

Node's WebSocket reports a failed connection with only an error event and
leaves the socket CONNECTING, where browsers follow the error with close. A
server script that reconnects from onclose (the usual pattern) then stopped
retrying for good. The wrapper now closes a socket that errors before it
opened, once, so scripts see the same events on the server and on clients.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018ds2NZXw5KLxDpVm9B3ABD
